## Read-only rootfs implications
- Scripts, configs, recorded video → /mnt/userfs (rw)
- Package installs / writes to /usr need remount rw
- WiFi credentials: bake into image or keep on userfs

## Remote update strategy (WiFi only, U-Boot has no WiFi)
- USB (uuu, SDP or fastboot): U-Boot, GPT, full reflash — local only
- Over SSH: kernel/DTB by writing p1 (unmounted), e.g. `cat bootfs.ext4 | ssh root@ip "dd of=/dev/mmcblk0p1 bs=1M && sync"`
- Possible later: package feed (needs VirtualBox Bridged adapter), A/B rootfs (RAUC/SWUpdate)
- scp from Ubuntu 24.04 to dropbear needs `scp -O`

